The reference probe is traceable to the national standard through the accredited laboratory Thermetrix Kalibracja Sp. z o.o. in Gdańsk (the certificate named above). The certificate is valid for 12 months and the next calibration of the probe is due in February 2025.

## 3. Results — temperature

Offset = reading of the device minus reference. All values in °C.

| Point | Reference (°C) | Offset as found | Offset after adjustment | Limit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | +40.0 | _____ | _____ | ±0.25 as found; ±0.10 after adjustment |
| 2 | 0.0 | _____ | _____ | ±0.25 as found; ±0.10 after adjustment |
| 3 | −25.0 | _____ | _____ | ±0.25 as found; ±0.10 after adjustment |

For KC-Tag 4 R1 devices the as-found limit is ±0.40 °C.

## 4. Results — humidity

| Point | Reference (% RH) | Offset as found (% RH) | Offset after adjustment (% RH) | Limit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 11.3 | _____ | _____ | ±2.0 |
| 2 | 75.3 | _____ | _____ | ±2.0 |

Humidity points are adjusted only when the customer needs humidity (see the service manual KC-SM-4, chapter 7.4).

## 5. Statement

☐ As found: within limits, no adjustment made.
☐ Adjusted: offsets written to the device, re-measured within limits.
☐ Rejected: see rejection report (sensor board replaced, calibration repeated).

The expanded uncertainty of measurement for the temperature points is ±0.08 °C (coverage factor k = 2, confidence level approximately 95 %). The statement of conformity is made with the simple acceptance rule: no guard band is applied.

Next calibration due*: ____.____.20___ (12 months after the date of calibration). The device displays the error E12 from 13 months after this date.

